.TH RUN 1 "August 2026" "Run Manual" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
run \- intelligent auto compiler, project runner, and developer productivity tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B run
[\fIfiles...\fR] [\fIoptions\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fIprogram-args...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B run
is a high-performance, intelligent build system and code runner. It automatically detects source languages (via file extension or shebang), compiles required binaries (C, C++, Rust, Java, Go, Zig), executes target programs with optional instrumentation, manages temporary artifacts, and supports custom workflows configured via \fBRun.toml\fR.

.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Execution & Runtime"
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch
Watch mode: monitor target files and dependencies, re-compiling and re-running automatically upon file change. Press \fBc\fR or Enter to trigger manual rebuilds.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Force continue on errors and disable interactive prompts.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry-run
Simulate compilation and execution without running commands.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time
Measure and display total program execution time in seconds.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-mem ", " \-\-memory
Measure and display peak resident memory usage (RSS). Can be combined with \fB-t\fR (e.g., \fBrun solution.cpp -tM\fR).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Silence compiler output and info banners.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-vv ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose debug logging (\fB-v\fR) or full trace with exception stack traces (\fB-vv\fR).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-stdin " [\fIfile\fR]"
Redirect standard input from a file or from a piped shell stream (e.g. \fBecho "data" | run test.py -i\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-expect " file"
Verify program output against an expected answer file. Displays colored unified diffs on mismatch.
.TP
.BI \-\-test\-dir " directory"
Batch testcase runner: discovers and executes all matching testcase pairs (\fB*.in\fR + \fB*.out\fR or \fBin*.txt\fR + \fBout*.txt\fR) in the specified folder and displays a summary table.
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Multi-language smart debugger launcher. Automatically uses \fBlldb\fR on macOS, \fBgdb\fR on Linux, \fBpdb\fR for Python, and \fB--inspect-brk\fR for Node.js.
.TP
.BR \-\-gdb
Compile and attach an interactive GDB debugger session.
.TP
.BR \-\-lldb
Compile and attach an interactive LLDB debugger session.
.TP
.BR \-\-valgrind
Run compiled binary with Valgrind detailed memory leak checking (\fB--leak-check=full --track-origins=yes\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
Set maximum execution time limit before terminating the process.
.TP
.BI \-\-env " KEY=VALUE"
Set environment variable for the child process. Can be passed multiple times.
.TP
.BI \-\-argument " args"
Arguments to pass to the compiled binary or script. Alternatively, pass arguments after a \fB--\fR separator.

.SS "Security & Isolation"
.TP
.BR \-\-restrict
Run with native OS sandboxing/isolation (Bubblewrap on Linux, setrlimit on macOS).
.TP
.BR \-\-sandbox
Compile and run inside an isolated Docker/Podman container environment.
.TP
.BR \-\-sandbox\-net
Allow network access inside the sandboxed container or bubblewrap environment.

.SS "Compilation & Build"
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-multi
Compile multiple source files together into a single binary. Includes CPM (C Project Manager) to automatically detect \fBmain()\fR entrypoint.
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-preset " name"
Apply a build preset defined in \fBRun.toml\fR (e.g., \fBdebug\fR, \fBrelease\fR).
.TP
.BI \-j ", " \-\-jobs " N"
Number of parallel worker threads to utilize for multi-file compilation.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-build\-only ", " \-\-no\-run
Compile or build the binary without executing it (preserves the binary).
.TP
.BR \-\-asan
Compile with AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer flags (\fB-fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-tsan
Compile with ThreadSanitizer flags (\fB-fsanitize=thread\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-sanitize " type"
Compile with arbitrary custom sanitizer flags (\fB-fsanitize=\fItype\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-link\-auto " [depth]"
Auto-discover and link all source files in the project workspace up to an optional search depth.
.TP
.BI \-\-flags " flags"
Pass custom compiler or interpreter flags (e.g. \fB--flags="-Wall -O3"\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-compiler " binary"
Override compiler or interpreter executable (e.g. \fB--compiler clang++\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-out\-dir " directory"
Output directory where compiled binaries will be placed.
.TP
.BR \-\-keep
Preserve compiled binaries after execution instead of deleting them.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-cache
Bypass compilation caching and force full recompilation.

.SS "Project & Utilities"
.TP
.BI \-\-new " target"
Scaffold starter source code or multi-file project templates.
.TP
.BI \-\-template " name"
Specify a named template defined in \fBRun.toml\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-doctor
Run system toolchain diagnostics across compilers, interpreters, and build utilities.
.TP
.BR \-\-init
Initialize a tailored \fBRun.toml\fR configuration file for the current project.
.TP
.BI \-\-directory ", " \-\-cwd " directory"
Change working directory before executing.
.TP
.BR \-\-clean
Clear the local compilation cache.
.TP
.BI \-\-completion " [shell]"
Generate shell completion script for \fBzsh\fR, \fBbash\fR, \fBfish\fR, or \fBpowershell\fR. When called without arguments, prints setup instructions.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color formatting in terminal output (also respects \fBNO_COLOR\fR env var).
.TP
.BR \-\-unsafe
Allow running as root (caution).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show installed version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display short help message and exit.

.SH CONFIGURATION
\fBrun\fR reads configuration from \fBRun.toml\fR. It searches for configuration files in the following priority order:
.IP 1. 3
Current working directory or any parent directory (up to 4 levels up).
.IP 2. 3
Global configuration directory:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/run_kuranne/Run.toml\fR or \fB~/.config/run_kuranne/Run.toml\fR on Linux/macOS.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB%APPDATA%\\run_kuranne\\Run.toml\fR on Windows.
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set and non-empty, suppresses ANSI color formatting.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Specifies location of user-specific global configuration files.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Specifies location of compilation caches.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B run solution.cpp -tM -i input.txt
Compile and benchmark execution time, peak memory, with input redirection.
.TP
.B run solution.cpp --test-dir ./tests/ -tM
Execute all testcase pairs in the tests directory.
.TP
.B run main.cpp --debug
Launch an interactive debugging session (LLDB on macOS, GDB on Linux).
.TP
.B run --new solution.cpp
Scaffold a starter C++ solution file.
.TP
.B run --new ./problem1 --template leetcode_rs
Scaffold a multi-file LeetCode template (\fBmain.rs\fR + \fBsolve.rs\fR).
.TP
.B run --doctor
Diagnose all installed toolchains and runtimes.

